<title>USA: Provident American says unit rating raised.</title>
<headline>Provident American says unit rating raised.</headline>
<dateline>NORRISTOWN, Pa. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Provident American Corp said Tuesday A.M. Best upgraded the rating of the company's primary insurance subsidiary, Provident Indemnity Life Insurance Co, to &quot;B&quot; from &quot;B-minus&quot;.</p>
<p>The company said A.M. Best, a rating service for insurance companies, also assigned the same upgraded group rating to Provident American Life &amp; Health Insurance Co, its new wholly owned subsidiary.</p>
<p>It said the &quot;B&quot; rating now applies in all 42 states in which Provident American is licensed to do business.</p>
</text>
